<title>USA: LCS to take $1 mln charge for write-off.</title>
<headline>LCS to take $1 mln charge for write-off.</headline>
<dateline>CLIFTON, N.J. 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>LCS Industries Inc said Monday it will take a $1 million one-time charge to its net income after deciding to write off its entire investment in McIntyre &amp; King Ltd.</p>
<p>LCS President Arnold Scheine said in a news release the action &quot;should have only a slight impact on our financial position.&quot;</p>
<p>McIntyre is a United Kingdom-based telemarketing, fulfillment and mailing services company.</p>
<p>LCS is a direct-response marketing services company. Its shares closed up 7/8 to 17-1/8 on Monday.</p>
</text>
